From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:01:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell: Default the graphics stolen memory to 32
 MiB

The gfx_uma_size option of the native RAM init defaulted to 64 MiB, the
size the code reserved before the option existed, while mrc.bin reserves
a fixed 32 MiB: the two variants of the same board booted with different
memory maps unless the option was set by hand. 32 MiB holds the firmware
framebuffer at the panel's full resolution (18.7 MB at 2880x1620) and is
the size the OpenCore configuration of the W541 was made for, so the
same configuration now works on both variants. Linux and Windows take
graphics memory from the system RAM through the GTT and are not limited
by the stolen size. The values offered do not change; a saved setting is
kept, only a store without one gets the new default.

TEST=Applied on the series; not built. On a W541 with the native RAM
init and no gfx_uma_size variable, the coreboot log must show GGC with
GMS 1 (32 MiB) and the memory map a 32 MiB stolen area, and the setup
must show 32 MB as the default.
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/cfr.h        | 4 ++--
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c | 6 +++---
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/cfr.h b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/cfr.h
index 4133f6acbb..4a1bbad2c4 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/cfr.h
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/cfr.h
@@ -34,8 +34,8 @@ static const struct sm_object gfx_uma_size = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.ui_helptext	= "Memory reserved at boot for the integrated GPU (graphics\n"
 			  "stolen memory), taken from system RAM. Takes effect at the\n"
 			  "next boot.\n"
-			  "Default: 64 MB.",
-	.default_value	= IGD_UMA_SIZE_64MB,
+			  "Default: 32 MB, what mrc.bin reserves.",
+	.default_value	= IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB,
 	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
 				{ "32 MB",	IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB	},
 				{ "64 MB",	IGD_UMA_SIZE_64MB	},
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
index 59d334fad0..8dfda0ff24 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/early_init.c
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ u8 haswell_igd_gms(void)
 	if (!CONFIG(USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT))
 		return IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB;
 
-	const unsigned int gms = get_uint_option("gfx_uma_size", IGD_UMA_SIZE_64MB);
+	const unsigned int gms = get_uint_option("gfx_uma_size", IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB);
 	switch (gms) {
 	case IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB:
 	case IGD_UMA_SIZE_64MB:
@@ -52,8 +52,8 @@ u8 haswell_igd_gms(void)
 	case IGD_UMA_SIZE_512MB:
 		return gms;
 	default:
-		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "IGD: invalid gfx_uma_size %u, using 64 MiB\n", gms);
-		return IGD_UMA_SIZE_64MB;
+		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "IGD: invalid gfx_uma_size %u, using 32 MiB\n", gms);
+		return IGD_UMA_SIZE_32MB;
 	}
 }
 
